{
  "title": "Why Groundnuts Deserve A Spot In Your Daily Diet \u2013 5 Health Benefits You Must Know",
  "publication_date": "2025-04-17T12:34:55Z",
  "summary": "Groundnuts (peanuts) are nutrient-rich legumes offering multiple health benefits. They contain healthy fats that reduce heart disease risk, provide plant-based protein, promote weight management through satiety, contain antioxidants for skin health, and support brain function through essential nutrients.",
  "content": "Groundnuts, also known as peanuts, are more than just a crunchy snack. Packed with protein, fibre, and essential nutrients, these tiny legumes can do wonders for your health. If you're searching for a simple, budget-friendly superfood, groundnuts are your answer.\n\nGroundnuts are rich in monounsaturated and polyunsaturated fats, which help lower bad cholesterol and reduce heart disease risk.\n\nA handful of groundnuts provides plant-based protein, supporting muscle growth and repair.\n\nHigh fibre and protein content promote satiety, helping control cravings and maintain a healthy weight.\n\nGroundnuts contain resveratrol and vitamin E, which fight oxidative stress and support skin health.\n\nNiacin and folate in groundnuts enhance memory and brain function.\n\nIncluding groundnuts in moderation can lead to a healthier, stronger you. Crunch your way to wellness today!",
